title: "AI Voice Agent for Appointment Booking | Zunkiree Labs" # SEOAI:TITLE
description: "An AI voice agent that answers your phone and takes the booking: live availability, written into your system, SMS confirmation, reschedules and reminders."
permalink: /solutions/voice-agent/
hideChrome: true
bodyClass: "v2-inter"
faqs:
  - question: "Can it book into the calendar and system we already use?"
    answer: "That is the requirement that separates a demo from something useful, so it is where we start. The agent reads live availability from your system and writes the appointment back into it — no second diary for someone to reconcile. Where your booking rules are more complex than your calendar can express, Zennly sits between the two and resolves them."
  - question: "What stops it double-booking or offering a slot that does not exist?"
    answer: "Availability is never the model's judgement. The agent asks the scheduling engine what is bookable and can only offer what comes back, and the write is a transactional booking against the same engine — so two callers racing for the last slot cannot both get it. If the engine cannot confirm, the agent says so and offers alternatives rather than guessing."
  - question: "Will it reduce no-shows?"
    answer: "Two-way reminder calls are the mechanism — the caller can move the appointment during the call instead of silently not turning up, and a released slot can be offered to a waitlist. We would rather measure it on your own numbers than quote someone else's: we baseline your current no-show rate first, so the before-and-after is yours."
  - question: "What happens when the agent cannot handle a call?"
    answer: "It hands over, and the escalation rules are yours — by topic, by detected frustration, by caller, or on request. The person taking over gets the transcript and the detected intent, so the caller does not start again. A booking agent that cannot escalate cleanly is worse than no agent at all."
  - question: "Does it handle deposits or payment at the point of booking?"
    answer: "Where you already take payment through a provider we can integrate, yes — typically as a payment link sent by SMS during or straight after the call, which is both easier for the caller and safer than reading card details to an automated line. We would not recommend taking card numbers over a voice agent."
  - question: "What languages and accents does it handle?"
    answer: "English and Nepali are what we deploy most. What actually decides quality is not the language but your vocabulary and your callers' accents — treatment names, product codes, place names. So we test against recordings of your real calls before committing to a language, and tune on the terms that matter to you."
  - question: "Will callers know they are talking to an AI?"
    answer: "The agent says so at the start of the call, and we would push back on hiding it. In practice callers mind far less than people expect, because what they are comparing it against is a menu tree or a voicemail box. What they object to is not getting the appointment they rang for — which is the part worth engineering."
  - question: "How long does it take to get live?"
    answer: "It depends almost entirely on the booking system and the complexity of your availability rules, not on the voice part. We scope it by looking at your real calls and your actual constraints, and we will tell you up front if your rules are simple enough that a booking link would serve you better than a voice agent."
